{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449035-help-me-decide-on-the-clan-concept-and-theme","id":1449035,"title":"Help me decide on the clan, concept and theme!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-19T12:56:06-07:00","id":1449035,"title":"Help me decide on the clan, concept and theme!","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> So I'm joining a chronicle set in the Victorian Age in the the nordic regions, and the game rules used are the V20, V20DA, clanbooks and other revised material, but we're using the character creation model from V20DA, alongside this I have around 40 xp to develop the character further, and age-wise it's around the 100 year mark. The chronicle is Camarilla centric, though independent clans are also open.<br /> <br /> My problem is that I can't really decide on the clan, concept and theme because there is simply too many good and interesting ones to choose from, so to help me narrow down my choices I took a look at what disciplines I would like the character to based around and which supporting discipline I would like, furthermore I also wanted a fourth in-clan discipline through the merit additional discipline, which of course should be explainable/justifiable somehow. Currently I would like the concept and theme to be more centric to being a magus of a sort<br /> Though, it's of importance to note that I would it like to preferably be having a norse/nordic angle to it. I'm open to other compelling suggestions, but do bear in mind that it does have to fit with the chronicle taking place in a nordic region. To help you help me, I've assembled most of my work related to figuring out my options and the potential combinations, where disciplines on the list, are simply the ones I know I enjoy playing with and thus would prefer to have a character with some of these.<br /> <br /> Discipline Wishes + Clan Possibilities<br /> Animalism : Gangrel | Nosferatu | Ravnos | Tzimisce)<br /> Chimerstry : Ravnos | Nephilim<br /> Dominate : Giovanni | Lasombra | Tremere | Ventrue | Malkavian (Dominate)<br /> Necromancy : Giovanni<br /> Obfuscate : Assamite: Warrior | Follower of Set | Malkavian | Nosferatu | Gangrel(City/Greek)<br /> Potence : Brujah | Giovanni | Lasombra, Nosferatu<br /> Presence : Assamite: Vizier | Brujah | Follower of Set | Toreador | Ventrue<br /> Thaumaturgy: Assamite: Sorcerer | Tremere<br /> (Blood Sorcery Equivalent)<br /> <br /> Quietus isn't on the list, but it's one of those that could be nice to have, I make note of it here since Assamite is on the list above, and could have a bearing on the final decision.<br /> Considerations with regards to the most common ones which aren't on the list: Celerity and Fortitude, these aren't completely out of the question, if the concept and theme would benefit from these as in-clan rather than and out of clan, then I would be open to consider these as well.<br /> Obtenebration, was also one actually considered, but since the chronicle already has several users of this one, I thought I'd skip it.<br /> <br /> With that being said, I know that I really would like the character to have Thaumaturgy or an equivalent of such and Necromancy, but this means that it's either Giovanni, Cappadocian, Tremere, Assamite: Sorcerer if which ever of two discplines missing is added through the additional discipline merit. Of these, the &quot;strongest&quot; candidate by far would be Giovanni, as it already has three of the ones thats on the list, but I don't really know if I want to be playing a Giovanni for this chronicle, especially because I'm not sure if and how I can make the norse/nordic theme fit with the lore of the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> If we're looking at which has just at least three of the ones as in-clan disciplines including if added through the additional discipline merit, but not necessarily a blood sorcery discipline as a clan discipline to start with. This broadens the list of potential clans to choose from significantly, at the sacrifice of only starting with one of the two blood sorcery disciplines I wanted, which also opens the question, if only one of these, then which one? Other supporting disciplines on the list, could be added as out of clan, though it would make most sense if it was non-signature clan disciplines.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, this means that the following clans and bloodlines with the discipline combinations would be:<br /> Brujah: Potence | Presence | Thaumaturgy or Necromancy.<br /> Lasombra Antitribu: Obtenebration | Dominate | Potence | Necromancy or Thaumaturgy - The chronicle already has several of these, so skipping this one, even though it could be cool.<br /> Malkavian (Dominate): Dominate | Obfuscate | Necromancy or Thaumaturgy<br /> Nosferatu: Animalism | Obfuscate | Potence | Necromancy or Thaumaturgy<br /> Ravnos: Animalism | Chimerstry | Fortitude | Necromancy or Thaumaturgy<br /> Nephilim: Auspex | Chimerstry | Presence | Necromancy or Thaumaturgy<br /> Ventrue: Dominate | Fortitude | Presence | Necromancy or Thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> The strongest one of the ones with direct access to a blood sorcery equivalent and their combination:<br /> Giovanni: Dominate | Potence | Necromancy | Thaumaturgy<br /> Tremere: Auspex | Dominate | Thaumaturgy | Necromancy<br /> Cappadocian: Auspex | Fortitude | Necromancy (Mortis) | Thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> This one is potentially among the top picks, but depending on which edition I choose from, will change it's clan disciplines, and would most likely be subject to further justification.<br /> Assamite: Sorcerer:<br /> - VTM Assamite Sorcery | Obfuscate | Quietus | Necromancy<br /> - VTDA - Assamite Sorcery | Auspex | Quietus | Necromancy or other from list<br /> - V20DA - Assamite Sorcery | Auspex | Celerity | Necromancy or other from list<br /> <br /> Technically, Caitiff or bloodline progenitor could also be an option, although I don't want to just be playing a nice set of disciplines and abilities, but actually be playing a character with depth, meaning and importance to the game and character story.<br /> <br /> As mentioned before, I'm open to compelling suggestions, I'm certainly not against playing a character with only access to one blood sorcery equivalent, but should be fairly centric to the theme. As you probably can tell by now, there are so many options available, hence why I need a bit of help deciding. And of course, feel free to use this for when figuring out potential character concepts based around disciplines.<br /> <br /> Some of the concepts I've been working with, as a one line inspiration:<br /> <br /> Concept #1 - The Nordic Magus (A viking mage equivalent)<br /> Concept #2 - Bloodline Experimentation<br /> Concept #3 - Master of Illusion and Manipulation<br /> Concept #4 - Master of Ravens and the Dead<br /> Concept #5 - Priest/Crusader of Corruption<br /> Concept #6 - The Burned Nosferatu<br /> Concept #7 - The Highwayman<br /> Concept #8 - The Twisted Ventrue<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading, and if you decide to to pitch in and help, thank you, it's much appreciated.<br /> <br /> // Inc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T13:41:50-07:00","id":1449044,"title":"","content":"Brrrr. Too much text. You make it hard to help you. <br /> <br /> Just play a Tremere. <br /> Or A Settite. <br /> Those are your best options for magic, and they're generally always good options so long as your ST is willing to deal with thaumaturgy. Also good options if you want to play a priest. Also good options if you want to get into &quot;viking&quot; stuff (which is very anachronistic given the time period so I'd advice against it, but you can do you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T14:05:12-07:00","id":1449047,"title":"","content":"I say play a Brujah with Necromancy. But I'm partial: Brujah have Necromancy as an in-clan discipline in my homebrew rules. And go with the Twisted Ventrue concept -- but not Ventrue. A regal, noble, powerful Brujah with a sick, twisted fascination with death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T19:01:42-07:00","id":1449075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449035-help-me-decide-on-the-clan-concept-and-theme?p=1449044#post1449044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brrrr. Too much text. You make it hard to help you.<br /> <br /> Just play a Tremere.<br /> Or A Settite.<br /> Those are your best options for magic, and they're generally always good options so long as your ST is willing to deal with thaumaturgy. Also good options if you want to play a priest. Also good options if you want to get into &quot;viking&quot; stuff (which is very anachronistic given the time period so I'd advice against it, but you can do you.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea with the &quot;viking&quot;-part, was more to emulate the theme, even though it may not really fit with the current time period, however it was the intention to make fitting changes to the character that would reflect that it had adapted to the time period. Also, a Follower of Set could make sense as the clan is in the north, however the clan doesn't sit well with the ST, and personally I'm not really a fan of Serpentis. With the Tremere part, it's definitely an option and I did actually begin making it around that before I began exploring other option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","user":"Incarnate","date":". 05-19-2021, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T19:13:42-07:00","id":1449076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449035-help-me-decide-on-the-clan-concept-and-theme?p=1449047#post1449047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say play a Brujah with Necromancy. But I'm partial: Brujah have Necromancy as an in-clan discipline in my homebrew rules. And go with the Twisted Ventrue concept -- but not Ventrue. A regal, noble, powerful Brujah with a sick, twisted fascination with death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite interesting concept and underlying theme, this could possibly be tweaked a bit further, other a few other clans could be as a the basis of it, but I do like it as is.<br /> Adding dominate to the mix would make it be much closer that of a Ventrue, without their feeding restrictions, and IF one were to couple it with animalism, then he could essentially be using animals as his army and spies, and who ever die to him could be raised as warriors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T16:27:40-07:00","id":1449217,"title":"","content":"Ravnos.<br /> <br /> The clan traditionally divides itself into a number of lineages known as Jati (an Indian term that refers to lineage, kinship group and caste). One of the ones I use in my own games, the Seidr, originate from the Nordic and German areas and are based around the cultural concepts of female seers/wisewomen (volva/spakona) and witchcraft (Seidr). They're descended from the original Indian Brahman caste bloodline (what the Roma Ravnos would call Phuri Dae, but I just call Seers) and so have Auspex as a clan discipline in place of Fortitude. This plays into both the traditional Germanic folklore about seers as well as the powers/magics traditionally associated with Seidr in Norse folklore/mythology (illusions, mind reading, astral projection, and being able to project ones consciousness into animals). This can be augmented by vampire runic blood magic (described in the Dark Ages book Wolves of the Sea; it used mortal Sorcery paths IIRC, but I just adapt Thaumaturgy for it, using paths like Spirit Manipulation, Warding, and Weather Control).<br /> (While Seidr is traditionally a woman's art, it is practiced by men, and while my Jati is majority female, it's not gender exclusive or anything.)<br /> <br /> <br /> (rough draft with no XP spent)<br /> Concept: Nordic Seidr Witch<br /> Clan: Ravnos (Seer bloodline)<br /> <br /> Physical: 2/2/2 Social: 3/4/3 Mental 3/2/3<br /> Talents: Alertness 1, Awareness 2, Empathy 2, Intimidation 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> Skills: Animal Ken 2, Crafts 2, Etiquette 1, Larceny 2, Melee 1, Performance 2, Stealth 2, Survival 1<br /> Knowledge: Investigation 1, Medicine 2, Occult 4 (Nordic witchcraft)<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Animalism 1, Auspex 1, Chimerstry 1, +Runic Blood Magic (Path of Spirit Manipulation) 1<br /> Backgrounds: Herd 2, Influence 2, Retainers 3 (coven)<br /> <br /> Conscience 2 Self-Control 4 Courage 4<br /> Humanity 6<br /> Willpower 6","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 05-21-2021, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T16:10:48-07:00","id":1449493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449035-help-me-decide-on-the-clan-concept-and-theme?p=1449217#post1449217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos.<br /> <br /> The clan traditionally divides itself into a number of lineages known as Jati (an Indian term that refers to lineage, kinship group and caste). One of the ones I use in my own games, the Seidr, originate from the Nordic and German areas and are based around the cultural concepts of female seers/wisewomen (volva/spakona) and witchcraft (Seidr). They're descended from the original Indian Brahman caste bloodline (what the Roma Ravnos would call Phuri Dae, but I just call Seers) and so have Auspex as a clan discipline in place of Fortitude. This plays into both the traditional Germanic folklore about seers as well as the powers/magics traditionally associated with Seidr in Norse folklore/mythology (illusions, mind reading, astral projection, and being able to project ones consciousness into animals). This can be augmented by vampire runic blood magic (described in the Dark Ages book Wolves of the Sea; it used mortal Sorcery paths IIRC, but I just adapt Thaumaturgy for it, using paths like Spirit Manipulation, Warding, and Weather Control).<br /> (While Seidr is traditionally a woman's art, it is practiced by men, and while my Jati is majority female, it's not gender exclusive or anything.)<br /> <br /> <br /> (rough draft with no XP spent)<br /> Concept: Nordic Seidr Witch<br /> Clan: Ravnos (Seer bloodline)<br /> <br /> Physical: 2/2/2 Social: 3/4/3 Mental 3/2/3<br /> Talents: Alertness 1, Awareness 2, Empathy 2, Intimidation 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> Skills: Animal Ken 2, Crafts 2, Etiquette 1, Larceny 2, Melee 1, Performance 2, Stealth 2, Survival 1<br /> Knowledge: Investigation 1, Medicine 2, Occult 4 (Nordic witchcraft)<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Animalism 1, Auspex 1, Chimerstry 1, +Runic Blood Magic (Path of Spirit Manipulation) 1<br /> Backgrounds: Herd 2, Influence 2, Retainers 3 (coven)<br /> <br /> Conscience 2 Self-Control 4 Courage 4<br /> Humanity 6<br /> Willpower 6</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your suggestion, it sounds quite interesting, unfortunately this has bloodline written all over the place, which I'm fairly sure the ST will not allow the players to use, and most definitely would not be allowed to use something that is homebrew (essentially custom versions of the paths), but perhaps something similar could be achieved with vanilla material. Since this is a bloodline, what clan weakness does it have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T23:12:37-07:00","id":1449514,"title":"","content":"They are a variation/subset of the Ravnos Clan detailed in both their revised ed Clanbook and the Dark Ages Libellus Sanguinus 4: Thieves in the Night, as well as the revised ed corebook. They have the exact same weakness as every other Ravnos. The only home made part is the culture, which is entirely taken from real world history and folklore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T17:12:20-07:00","id":1450520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449035-help-me-decide-on-the-clan-concept-and-theme?p=1449514#post1449514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are a variation/subset of the Ravnos Clan detailed in both their revised ed Clanbook and the Dark Ages Libellus Sanguinus 4: Thieves in the Night, as well as the revised ed corebook. They have the exact same weakness as every other Ravnos. The only home made part is the culture, which is entirely taken from real world history and folklore.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's an established variation of the clan, then that part probably wont be a problem.<br /> But I don't really see the vampire runic blood magic described in the book: Wolves at the Sea, as you described, the only thing I found was a merit that allows you to take mortal sorcery paths from the Sorcery book, also there are some restrictions as to which paths cannot be learned and that one may not learn Thaumaturgy paths and without having learned it as a discipline in the regular fashion. So I'm unsure if you were basing the runic magic connection through this merit, or just adapting Thaumaturgy to fit with the theme, but it does sound customized - I still like it quite a lot, but with the custom nature, I probably won't be able to get that part approved. But even it doesn't. it's definitely one I'd like to try out some time.<br /> <br /> Last I spoke with the STs, we were discussing a potential Assamite angle, but he weren't too keen on an Assamite sorcerer, because it wouldn't be very likely for an Assamite sorcerer to be in Scandinavian lands, as in it wouldn't have very plausible reasons for being there. I'm sure there could be plenty of reasons. Either way, I was told, the only way I would be able to get access to Assamite sorcery, would be if I was playing an Assamite Warrior or Vizier, who had earned it and was taught it in-game. To me that seems quite restrictive, I was basically told, that if I wanted to play a mage, I should just be playing a Tremere, but there is already one Tremere player in the chronicle not to mention the npcs as well, speaking of the chronicle - it's taking place in a open world sandbox style game (though with narratives and plots) thats being run online with many players, and the players aren't necessarily part of a coterie or the same if in a coterie. There was several reasons, one being Tremere and Assamites don't get along and the second being that a sorcerer would easily be identified because of it's weakness. With that being said, I don't think it's likely that I would be allowed to add Thaumaturgy or Necromancy, to any character in character creation that doesn't normally have access to Thaumaturgy or an equivalent, or Necromancy, at least not without a very compelling reason.<br /> <br /> This obviously rules out the majority of the possible clans from the list of approved (see below) clans for play in their chronicle.<br /> <br /> An angle I can see for an Assamite sorcerer or a warrior or vizier that might earn the &quot;right&quot; to be taught their sorcery through play, would be one that is the lands to search for demons and rid them from existence should they be discovered - a mentor with a telepathic connection established through a ritual to the character, would help guide and once they've been found, begin the process of teaching sorcery to the character - something down those lines.<br /> <br /> As mentioned before, the main requirement is having access to blood magic: Thaumaturgy or it's equivalents or Necromancy.<br /> Clans currently approved for players to choose from (no bloodlines and clans with zero slots have been excluded):<br /> Assamite (obviously with some restrictions.)<br /> Brujah<br /> Followers of set<br /> Gangrel (which includes City variant)<br /> Giovanni<br /> Malkavian<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Ravnos<br /> Tremere<br /> Toreador<br /> Ventrue<br /> <br /> Note: As far as I understand, the amount of slots, has been based on the likelihood of members of the clan being in the Scandinavian land.<br /> 2nd Note: Giovanni and Tremere clans already has several players under their banners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","user":"Incarnate","date":". 06-01-2021, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24617-incarnate","name":"Incarnate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T00:39:40-07:00","id":1451120,"title":"","content":"About concept. I know the viking thing is exciting, but during the 1700s there weren't really that much &quot;Viking stock&quot; to choose from.<br /> In that case I'd choose a Nosferatu, since they had many of your preferred disciplines, and make it the child of an old Viking era witch.<br /> But have fun with the background before the elder Nosferatu picked out your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1914-davidiot","name":"davidiot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T12:02:31-07:00","id":1451156,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, the Giovanni do not restrict their overall membership solely to those belonging to their original bloodline. The Giovanni are always on the lookout for other groups having something to offer their clan. Thus we have the lesser Giovanni bloodlines such as the Scottish Dunsirns, the Mexican Pisonab line and the Miliners of the United States - just to name a few. A little research into the Nordic mythologies reveals the death cult of Hel, who await the construction of Naglfar, a boat made entirely from the fingernails and toenails of the dead which Hel shall use upon it's completion in the Final Nights to ferry her army of wraiths.<br /> <br /> Sounds very close to the Giovanni goal of collecting enough souls to bring about the Endless Night. The Giovanni would likely be quite eager to incorporate such a labor towards the advancement of their own agenda. Not to mention the prospect of adding into their necromantic repertoire a possible new path centered around the fabrication of powerful items from the bodies of the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":19671,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19671-dgs-chad","user":"DGS-Chad","date":". 06-06-2021, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19671-dgs-chad","name":"DGS-Chad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}